    {
      "title": "Yemen officials blame Houthis for 2 missile strikes on Yemen's Aden airport",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/yemen-officials-blame-houthis-for-2-missile-strikes-on-yemen-s-aden-airport-126101700052_1.html",
      "description": "Two missiles struck the airport in Yemen's port city of Aden on Friday night, police said, blaming Iran-backed Houthi rebels for the second such attack in less than a week.\nPolice said no casualties were reported as fighting escalates in the latest front in the Iran war, one in which the rebels have attacked both neighbouring Saudi Arabia and Yemen's internationally recognized government that's backed by the kingdom.\nA security official and a traffic controller said an area of the Aden airport that hosts a military unit aligned with the Saudi-backed government was hit. Both spoke on condition of anonymity because they were not authorized to speak to the media.\nThere was no immediate claim of responsibility.\nThe attack came a day after the Houthis carried out a deadly strike on a palace complex in Aden, which has been the seat of the internationally recognized government since 2015.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-17T02:27:00"
    }
